esson_name"}, {"content": "The First Shift", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe taste and style in music and fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Position of Not", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In English, the adverb  <span class=\"italic\">not</span> usually goes after the auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d to form the negative. <br/><br/> You can use the adverb <span class=\"italic\">not </span>in other positions in some cases.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, we find the adverb <span class=\"italic\">not</span> in conjunction with an auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d in a negative sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">He's <span class=\"strong\">not</span> going to be able to make it.</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">That will <span class=\"strong\">not</span> be disappointing.</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">People don't like to feel rushed = People do <span class=\"strong\">not</span> like to feel rushed.</span><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the long form instead of the contraction, you emphasize the negation of the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You also find <span class=\"italic\">not</span> <span class=\"strong\">before</span> a verb in the Infinitive.<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I can tell you what not to do.<br/> I will try not to get on their nerves.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/>         The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to dress up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to wear elegant clothes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to respond in an impolite way\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to put up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to tolerate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look down on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to feel superior to someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to respect someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to hang around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to spend time with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to get by with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to manage with little effort\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to wait on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to serve in a restaurant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to fill in for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to replace someone\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " I'd like you to fill in for our waiter tonight. Do you feel up to it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think you can get by with what you know at this point.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to dress up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to wear elegant clothes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People like to dress up on Saturday nights.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you work in a restaurant.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get by with ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to manage with little effort", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think you can get by with what you know at this point.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to wait on ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to serve in a restaurant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're going to wait on some important customers tonight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fill in for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to substitute for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mike can't make it, so Joe is going to fill in for him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fashion-conscious ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " always aware of how their clothes look", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Models are extremely fashion-conscious.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "theater crowd", "type": "name"}, {"content": "people who love to go to the theater", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Saturday nights are popular with the theater crowd.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dressed to the nines", "type": "name"}, {"content": " dressed very elaborately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wow. A tuxedo, cane and top hat. You really dressed to the nines.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a dialogue about a night out at a trendy restaurant/pub.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the phrasal verbs from this lesson.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make the dialogue 6-8 sentences long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Dictate your dialogue to a group. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your partners must write down the gist of your story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Next, work together to fill in the missing grammar details. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "After 10 minutes, compare their dialogue to yours.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners and customs. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about life experiences. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my opinion. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I  listen for gist.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I add grammar details.", "type": "text"}]}]}